          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The extended probabilistic powerdomain is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad+of+valuations"} monad of valuations
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            the space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+valuations"} continuous valuations
            over it.
          %p
            The idea of this monad was first given by Kirch for the case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domains"} domains
            (see
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#kirch"} Kirch ‘93
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Jung"} AJK ‘06
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            and given its current form by Heckmann (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Heckmann96"} Heckmann ‘96
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#spaces_of_valuations Spaces of valuations
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V X
            the space whose points are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+valuations"} continuous valuations
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with values in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,\infty]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V X
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+basis"} generated
            by the sets in the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi ν
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi V
                  %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi ν
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\theta(U,r) \coloneqq \{ \nu \in V X \,|\, \nu(U) \gt r \},
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\ge 0
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\subseteq X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open"} open
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Θ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo ,
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mi ν
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi g
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi d
                    %mi ν
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mi r
                    %mo }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Theta(g,r) \coloneqq \left\{ \nu \in V X \,\Big|\, \int g \,d\nu \gt r \right\}
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\ge 0
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:X\to[0,\infty]
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lower+semicontinuous"} lower semicontinuous
          %p
            This topology can be seen as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointwise+topology"} pointwise topology
            if we view valuations either as functions on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+sets"} open sets
            or as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functionals"} functionals
            on lower semicontinuous functions (via
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+valuation#integration"} integration
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+topology"} initial topology
            of either evaluation of open sets or integration of functions, meaning that it is the coarsest topology for which either the assignments
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ν
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi ν
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\nu \mapsto \nu(U)
          %p
            for every open
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\subseteq X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ν
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo ∫
                  %mi g
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi d
                  %mi ν
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\nu \mapsto \int g \, d\nu
          %p
            for every lower semicontinuous
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:X\to[0,\infty]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+function"} measurability
            plays for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giry+monad"} Giry monad
            (see also
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence+between+measure+and+valuation+theory"} correspondence between measure and valuation theory
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/specialization+preorder"} specialization preorder
            of this topology is known as the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stochastic+order"} stochastic order
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointwise+order"} pointwise order
            of valuations as functions on the open sets.
          %p
            It is known (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#jung2"} Jung ‘04
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stably+compact"} stably compact
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V X
            is stably compact too, so that the monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            restrict to the subcategory of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stably+compact+spaces"} stably compact spaces
          %h3#functoriality Functoriality
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:X\to Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:V X\to V Y
            as the one assigning to a continuous valuation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ν
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi V
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu\in V X
            its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+valuation#pushforward"} pushforward
            along
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            It can be proven that the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V f
            is continuous too, so that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
          %h3#unit_and_multiplication Unit and multiplication
          %p
            We can define the unit of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            as follows. Given a space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta:X\to V X
            as the one assigning to the point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valuation+%28measure+theory%29#dirac_valuation"} Dirac valuation
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The multiplication map makes use of the concept of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valuation+%28measure+theory%29#integration"} integration over a valuation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                    %mi V
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi\in V V X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi V
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \xi\in V X
            as the one mapping an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open"} open
            set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\subseteq X
            to
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi X
                  %mi ν
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi d
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ν
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E \xi (U) \coloneqq \int_X \nu(U) \, d\xi(\nu).
          %p
            This integral is well defined, since the assignment
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi ν
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\mapsto \nu(U)
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lower+semicontinuous"} lower semicontinuous
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi E
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\mapsto E \xi (U)
            gives a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+valuation"} continuous valuation
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mi V
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E: V V X \to V X
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            satisfy the usual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axioms"} axioms
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi δ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\delta,E)
            is usually called the
            = succeed "." do
              %strong extended probabilistic powerdomain
          %p
            This construction, especially the way the unit and multiplications are defined, can be thought of as a topological analogue of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giry+monad"} Giry monad
          %h2#monoidal_structure Monoidal structure
          %p (…)
          %h2#algebras Algebras
          %p (…)
          %h2#notable_submonads Notable submonads
          %p
            There are a number of monads that can be constructed as submonads of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+functor"} monoidal structure
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is inherited by these submonads too, allowing the formation of joints and marginals.
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads+of+probability%2C+measures%2C+and+valuations#detailed_list"} monads of probability, measures, and valuations - detailed list
          %h3#normalized_valuations Normalized valuations
          %p
            If one restricts to
            %em normalized
            valuations, i.e.~those
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ν
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi V
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu\in V X
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu(X)=1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            which can be thought of as the one of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability"} probability
            valuations.
          %h3#the_measure_monad_on_top The measure monad on Top
          %p
            One can restrict
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            only to those valuations which are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valuation+%28measure+theory%29#extending_valuations_to_measures"} extendable to measures
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi V
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M X\subseteq V X
            (for every topological space
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tau-additive+measures"} tau-additive measures
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
